<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Germany</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as German</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Germany is a country in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. Its lands formed the core of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a> and were unified in 1871 as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a>. Germany was the ally of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a> and later of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> in the world wars, and it figures in the histories of the Carolingian, Spanish and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-empire">Swedish Empires</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/germany.jpg" alt="Germany" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:SKopp, User:Madden, and other users · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Germany.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
